// lexdb over TDS: subquery unnesting, the second half (optimizer 51) through the T-SQL door, checked against SQL Server 2022
// (run with LEXDB_MSSQL set to its connection string, this test prints SQL Server's answers: the expect lines). A correlated
// scalar aggregate in WHERE, the select list and ORDER BY (COUNT, SUM, MAX, a key with no rows, an empty table, a varchar key
// under the session's case-insensitive collation, TOP), CROSS APPLY and OUTER APPLY over an aggregate with and without GROUP
// BY, an error in the expression over the aggregate where a key has no rows. Against lexdb each batch runs with the new
// levels and with the plans before them (lexdb_plan.setUnnest(7)) in this process: a difference is shown after the answer.
// The last line: how many batches the pipeline's joins ran with the new levels and how many with the plans before.
// expect: ok
